EducationBachelor's DegreeSkillsSQLNoSQLData ManagementXMLHadoopThe Company
ACTS has been a high-tech business partner and innovator for nearly two decades. Our customers are world class enterprises and consulting organizations who span a diverse range of industries, verticals and geographies. Our deep Cloud expertise and long-standing relationships with Microsoft Field, Services and Delivery teams provide us with on-going insights and vision as Cloud Technologies evolve. ACTS is a leading Microsoft Cloud Solutions provider and Microsoft Gold Partner, recently named as Finalist for 2018 Microsoft Open Source Data & AI Partner of the Year, recognizing our innovative work in the areas of AI and Machine Learning.

We believe technology can reshape our clients’ businesses. We offer every client a unique perspective on technology, so they can recognize new business opportunities and make the most of them. Our most strategic technology partner - Microsoft plays a pivotal role in our delivery of industry-disrupting, technology-driven solutions to clients.

Our approach is to provide clients with technology-enabled solutions that deliver sustainable business value in areas such as application development, predictive analytics, machine learning, cloud computing, artificial intelligence, digital integration, IoT and managed services.

Scope of the Job
We are looking for a Data and Advanced Analytics Consultant specialized in the Microsoft Data and AI eco-system to include: Data Architecture, Big Data, Data Platform, Business Intelligence, Data Science/Machine Learning and Data Visualization expertise with hands-on knowledge in these areas.

The ideal candidate will need to have experience in consulting with external customers delivering on Azure based solutions that drive strong business impact. Our team covers the entire life cycle of information utilization, from ideation through implementation.

Although our company headquarters is in Jacksonville, FL, this position can be remote and we'll look at candidates anywhere in the Southeast.

Essential Functions
Aware of modern relational and non-relational approaches of data stores as they relate to architectural/industry changes; especially in the areas of big data and the cloud-based solutions;
Assist with client facing cloud transformation and cloud readiness efforts related to enterprise information strategies of customer-focused enterprises and solutions;
Meeting with clients to determine needs and/or identify problem areas as they relate to information and data architecture;
Aware of information and data architecture modeling as it relates to information analysis, systems of record, categorization, information sensitivity, information exchange and data platforms;
Responsible for supporting the Modern data and analytics portfolio by working with customer and internal stakeholders (business clients, business analysts, developers, other architects), defining customer cloud solutions, and delivering engagements that are innovative and exceed business requirements;
Ability to blend quantitative and analytical skills, problem-solving and strategy consulting to engage the client in cloud-based solutions;
Understand the implementation of an IaaS, PaaS or SaaS based solution from end-to-end and the project artifacts for current and new service offerings along with the quality of the delivery to customers;
May be responsible for the development of resource estimates to support Statements of Work and Proposals which outline professional services required to meet client requirements;
Ability to communicate the status of architecture, development, quality, operations and system performance to internal stakeholders and external customers effectively;
Collaborate with other team members to develop and enhance deliverables; and
Continuously improve team processes to ensure information is of the highest quality, contributing to the overall effectiveness of the team.
Travel required

Skill and Qualifications
Experience with Azure cloud as it relates to data and information architecture;
Experience with cloud-based relational data stores, e.g., Azure SQL Database Service, Azure SQL Data Warehouse with polybase stored procedures;
Experience with cloud-based analytical services, e.g., Azure Analysis Services, Azure Data Lake Analytics, etc;
Experience with cloud-based non-relational data stores, e.g., Azure Blob Storage, Azure Data Lake Store, Azure CosmosDB, Azure HDInsight and Azure DataBricks;
Experience with Big Data Technology Stack (a plus): Hadoop/Spark/Hive/MapR;
Experience with data migration services, Azure Data Factory, Azure Data Catalog, EventHub, Stream Analytics, etc.;
Experience with Azure Logic Apps ans Azure Functions for real-time information exchange;
Experience with Azure Virtual Machines, StorSimple, Azure DNS, Virtual Network, Redis Cache, Azure App Service supporting service;
Extensive experience with information/data architecture modeling and developing client documentation;
Hands on .Net Technologies stack with SQL Data Tools (SSDT) and data visualization with PowerBI;
Strength and background in infrastructure or HPC (High Performance Computing) is preferable;
Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Computer Information System, Data Science, or similar discipline
5+ years experience with a Major BI Technology Sets;
5+ years experience in information architecture methodologies;
5+ years, recent experience developing solutions in a Microsoft SQL Server environment using SQL, T-SQL stored procedures, T-SQL functions; and/or an Oracle Environment using SQL Plus and PL/SQL Coding Languages as well as familiarity with complex SQL Server scaling concepts (AlwaysOn, Geo-Scaling, Sharding, Large Scale Database Management);
Knowledgeable in querying data stored using a broad range of data modeling techniques including third normal form, dimensional, and data vault modeling on Microsoft SQL Server-based technologies;
Experience designing and building cloud native applications as well as Azure Cloud migration experience;
Hands on experience in Azure, preferably data heavy/analytics applications leveraging relational and NoSQL databases, data warehouse and big data;
Experience with Azure IaaS and PaaS services;
Project experience using Azure cloud, data lake storage, installation, security and infrastructure (IaaS) set up;
Experience with Big Data Management (BDM) for relational and non-relational data (formats like json, xml, avro, parquet, copybook, etc.);
Performance tune complex ETL mappings for relational and non-relational workloads;
Advanced SQL programming, PL/SQL or T-SQL;
Knowledge of tabular OLAP, including PowerPivot and SSAS Tabular mode;
Knowledge of Microsoft Cortana Intelligence Suite;
Understanding of how traditional processes apply to the modern world (be able to talk about where big data and NoSQL can replace traditional enterprise data stores, how Azure Data Factory can supplement/replace SSIS, etc.);
Experience with the setup and configuration of PowerBI (Power Query, Data Management Gateway, SSAS Tabular Connector);
Experience implementing Master Data Services and Data Quality Services;
Exceptional customer engagement, interpersonal, presentation and overall communication skills;
Ability to successfully handle multiple work streams across multiple engagements, while maintaining composure and professionalism to meet tight deadlines and shifting priorities;
Quickly learn and adapt to new business and technical concepts;
Goal-oriented team player committed to quality and detail;
Innovative thinker who is positive, proactive and readily embraces change;
Strong understanding of Business Intelligence concepts and best practices, with an understanding of its strategic importance to organizations; and
Superior conceptual and analytical abilities, identifying opportunities for improvement through analysis and creative thinking.

