Participating on proposal development teams, including writing sections, coordinating efforts and preparing proposal submissions; and 
Other responsibilities, as necessary.

Description At Scripps Health, you will experience the pride, support and respect of an organization that has been repeatedly recognized as one of the nation’s Top 100 Places to Work.   You’ll be surrounded by people committed to making a difference in the lives of their patients and their teammates. So if you’re open to change, go ahead and unlock your potential.  The Principal Architect functions as an individual contributor and knowledge expert both within and outside the organization, acting as the primary technical expert in Scripps’ data platform, including data storage, data movement, data warehousing, data virtualization and business intelligence. Leads complex projects that span multiple disciplines and ensures the success of IT and business alignment. Perform large-scale IT program oversight. Contributes in the planning of the overall organizational IT strategy. Contributes to the overall health of the IT Portfolio. Develops %22new to industry%22 solutions for complex projects. Participates in industry/knowledge reference groups.  Ideal candidate for the Principal Architect role, has a substantive development, engineering and multi-platform architecture background, and simultaneously a desire to lead, grow and develop a true enterprise analytics strategic vision. This individual develops strong, credible relationships with all levels of team members and customers, and promotes the technology roadmap strategically in a way that both business and technical teams can understand and support.    Responsibilities:  Guide the overall enterprise data strategy for the Analytics team by creating, managing, and promoting the short and long-term analytics architectural vision that aligns with business goals; Establish and execute the vision and roadmap to drive the Analytics team forward technologically and strategically; Be the technical expert in Scripps’ data platform, including data storage, data movement, data warehousing, data virtualization and business intelligence Provide technical leadership, oversight and guidance to the Analytics team operationally, ensuring standards and best practices are in place and being followed; Collaborate with other principal and enterprise architects in Information Services to align analytics to the broader enterprise technical roadmap; Evaluate, recommend and establish new and emerging data storage, movement and management technologies and practices;  Ensure interoperability, scalability, performance and ROI of a cohesive system of infrastructure, data models, services and technologies that allow the Analytics team to produce high-value produce for customers enterprise-wide; Ensure compliance with data security and privacy standards and policies;    Lead the development of conceptual, logical and physical data assets to execute on high-value enterprise initiatives and engages with project managers, data architects, business partners, and senior leadership to ensure optimal solution is designed to meet business needs;   Function as principal Architect of a cohesive system of infrastructure, data models, services and technologies that allow the Analytics team to produce high-value produce for customers enterprise-wide; Translate industry technology direction to business value for key stakeholders; Advise during vendor selection and function as a critical component of build vs. buy decisions   This position will be at our newly designed, centrally San Diego located business services office, which offers an on-site café and gym. This is a full time, salaried position and offers Scripps Health’s award winning benefit package along with relocation assistance to those that qualify. QualificationsRequired Education/Experience/Specialized Skills:
