Arconic FasteningSystems (AFS) is looking for Salesand Marketing Analyst at our manufacturing plant in Waco, TX. Our Analyst will be responsible for creating salespresentations and marketing forecasts which support the S&OP process andsuccessful business plans.  Will gather data from multiple reliable sourcesto analyze market and customer trends to support revenue growth and profitenhancement; prepares detailed reports for senior managers in print, electronicformats and acts as an information resource to outside sales personnel. Arconic (NYSE: ARNC) creates breakthrough products that shapeindustries. Working in close partnership with our customers, we solve complexengineering challenges to transform the way we fly, drive, build and power.Through the ingenuity of our people and cutting-edge advanced manufacturingtechniques, we deliver these products at a quality and efficiency that ensurecustomer success and shareholder value.  Arconic Fastening Systems, abusiness unit of Arconic, holds the number one global position in aerospacefastening systems, and we’re the North American leader in commercialtransportation fasteners.  Our high-tech, multi-material fastening systemsare found nose to tail on aircraft and aero engines.  Our products arealso critical components of industrial gas turbines, automobiles, commercialtransportation vehicles, and construction and industrial equipment. Headquartered in Torrance, CA; AFS employs over 6,000 people in 11countries at 31 locations.Key Responsibilities:
Manages the preparation, compilation and update of the business plan and sales and marketing presentations for the Sales Leaders and VP of Sales and Marketing;
Consolidates build-rates, market trends and customer intelligence for the S&OP process, participates in the S&OP consensus forecast;
Contacts all major customers on a regular basis by phone or in-person and gathers build rates, forecasts, business conditions and other information. Maintains and updates associated contacts for major customers;
Prepare and update V.P & General Manager’s presentations, Industrial Hoshin, DI system updates and tracking;
Gathers, maintains and updates customer playbooks for top 20 customers: products, pricing, competitive analysis, strategic roadmap, negotiation support materials;
Prepares SIC and share gain reports on a monthly/quarterly/yearly basis;
Supports the Sales Leaders through ad-hoc sales and profitability analysis for customers, LOBs, products, etc. and preparation of presentations and other analytical material;
Supports RFA process with sales and profitability analysis;
Attends trade shows and conferences at Sales Leaders direction to gather market and competitive intelligence, maintain relationships with customers, compile and distribute sales leads;
Visits customers and distributors as required by Sales Leadership;
SPA for Phocus System, provides training on system as required, prepares customer/market/product/trend analysis as requires by Sales Leadership.
Additional Skills and Abilities:
Must be flexible to travel up to 25% of the time, including overnight as needed;
Will tour manufacturing environments and visit customer corporate locations;
Mathematical and statistical analytical skills using Excel and other tools;
Able to proficiently prepare professional presentations using PowerPoint;
Ability to function independently, take general directions and implement and execute a plan of action;
Comfortable functioning well in a high-paced environment under tight deadlines and balancing multiple competing priorities;
Comfortable presenting and participating in discussions within a high-level executive environment;
Understanding of accounting principles, profit, loss, standard costing, cash flow, net present value analysis.
