POSITION SUMMARY:The Sr. Strategy Analyst will report into the VP, Business Operations Support inclusive of Workforce Management, Reporting & Analytics, and Technology Management for Customer Relations. Customer Relations is a Customer Service and Collections organization. The Business Operations Support group is looking for a Senior Analyst who will be responsible for leveraging machine learning concepts to produce monthly forecasts and segmentation strategies.  Additionally, this role will have responsibilities around reporting, strategy enhancements, strategy development, model testing, implementation, validation and other ad hoc analytics for call forecasting, collection performance, and outbound campaign strategies to name a few.ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES:
Leverages machine learning concepts such as Linear, Logistic Regression, Random Forest, Boosting, etc. used to analyze business trends, create forecasts of performance, refine campaign strategies, etc. for actionable intelligence
Routinely validate statistical models w/ methodology including but not limited to split sample validation, KS Statistics, ROC Curves, and GINI.
Utilizing Scoring and Segmentation techniques, including the usage of Champion/Challenger design;
Develop Customer Contact Strategies, Digital Strategies, Segmentation, and Compliance Solutions reporting and analytics including tracking all changes with full documentation;
Provide analytic support and thought leadership to the team through the utilization of data mining skills and business knowledge for Customer Relations performance and other areas within Business Operations Support team;
Conduct analyses of accounts across all delinquency stages and portfolios. Leverage findings to drive collection effectiveness;
Support monthly forecast and planning processes related to operating drivers and expenses;
Perform ad-hoc analyses, as requested, with best practice standards of reporting and analysis;
Continuously streamline processes to eliminate inefficiencies and improve results across Customer Relations.
SKILLS/KNOWLEDGE/ABILITIES:
To effective use and build statistical models such as Linear, Logistic Regression, Random Forest, Boosting, etc. used to analyze business trends, create forecasts of performance, refine campaign strategies, etc. for actionable intelligence;
Ability to effectively communicate results in a concise manner for Executive level presentation;
Ability to identify issues of a complex nature and effectively resolve with data analysis and research;
Advanced PC skills; Microsoft Access, Excel, Word, Power Point, and other Database;
Strong working knowledge in presenting quantitative data via PowerPoint, Excel, Word, etc.
Strong Time Management abilities to adjust to fluctuating work load with the pressure of aggressive deadlines;
EDUCATION AND EXPERIENCE:
Bachelor's Degree - Business, Accounting, Mathematics, Statistics, or equivalent experience, with Master’s Degree Strongly Preferred;
5+ years’ experience in one of the following tools, SAS, R, or Python
3+ years’ experience in MS SQL
Experience using Business Objects and/or Tableau preferred.
